From 818ee7c934b2aba5c3c3d610b36ce005269068c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit <rohit@craftstudio.dev>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:53:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: stop artifact uploads exhausting storage quota

The CI failure on PR #1 was not a build failure. Every step through 'Build APK
without runtime' and 'APK size report' succeeded; only 'Upload artifacts' failed
with 'Artifact storage quota has been hit'.

Cause: each run uploaded out/* (release + debug + no-runtime APKs, ~450 MB) with
30-day retention. 28 live artifacts had accumulated to ~12.7 GB, over the quota
for a private repo on a user account.

The release and no-runtime APKs were also being stored twice, since the
'Create GitHub Release' step already publishes them as release assets
(confirmed on v3.38).

Changes:
- Skip artifact upload entirely on pull_request; the build steps already prove
  the code compiles
- On push/manual runs upload only the debug APK plus checksums, not the APKs
  that Releases already holds
- Drop retention 30 -> 7 days
- compression-level 0, since APKs are already ZIP containers
- Add 'synchronize' to pull_request types, so pushes to an open PR re-run CI.
  Previously only the first commit of a PR was ever built

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .github/workflows/android.yml | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/android.yml b/.github/workflows/android.yml
index 8150973..2ef3ab5 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/android.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/android.yml
@@ -6,7 +6,10 @@ on:
   pull_request:
     branches-ignore:
       - 'l10n_v3_openjdk'
-    types: [opened, reopened]
+    # 'synchronize' re-runs CI when new commits are pushed to an open PR.
+    # Without it only the very first commit was ever verified, so a PR could be
+    # merged green while its latest commit had never been built.
+    types: [opened, reopened, synchronize]
   workflow_dispatch:
 
 jobs:
@@ -144,13 +147,31 @@ jobs:
             echo "| $(basename $f) | $SIZE |" >> $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
           done
 
-      # ── Upload all artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
-      - name: Upload artifacts
+      # ── Upload artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+      # Storage notes: each run produced ~450 MB (three APKs plus checksums) and
+      # kept it for 30 days, which exhausted the repository's artifact quota and
+      # started failing every build.
+      #
+      # Two changes keep usage bounded:
+      #   1. Pull requests upload nothing. A PR only needs to prove the code
+      #      compiles, and the build steps above already do that.
+      #   2. Pushes and manual runs upload only the debug APK. The release and
+      #      no-runtime APKs are published to GitHub Releases by the next step,
+      #      so shipping them as artifacts too was storing the same file twice.
+      - name: Upload debug APK
         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'
         with:
           name: cs-launcher-v3-build-${{ github.run_number }}
-          path: out/*
-          retention-days: 30
+          path: |
+            out/CS-LAUNCHER-V3-DEBUG.apk
+            out/*.md5
+            out/*.sha256
+          retention-days: 7
+          # APKs are already ZIP containers, so recompressing them costs CI time
+          # for almost no size reduction.
+          compression-level: 0
+          if-no-files-found: warn
 
       # ── GitHub Release (manual only) ─────────────────────────────────────────
       - name: Create GitHub Release
-- 
2.39.5

